<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>CSS Position Practice</title>
  <style>
    .box{
        height: 200px;
        width:200px;
        background-color: #000000;
        position: fixed;
        
    }
    .box2{
        
        height: 200px;
        width:200px;
        background-color: blue;
        margin-top: 20px;
        position: fixed;
        top: 20px;
        right: 20px;
        
    }
    .long-text{
        float: right;
        margin-right: 20px;
           
    }
    
    
  </style>
</head>

<body>

  <h1 class="title">CSS Positioning Practice</h1>
  <h2>Hai developers</h2>

  <div id="first">
  <p class="para1">
    Web development involves structuring content using HTML and styling it using CSS.
    Understanding positioning helps developers control layout precisely.
  </p>
  </div>

  <div id="Second">
  <p class="para1">
    Relative positioning allows small adjustments without breaking the document flow.
    Absolute positioning is useful for placing elements exactly where needed.
  </p>
  </div>
  

  <!-- Parent box for absolute practice -->
   <div class="BlueBox_parent">
    <h2>HERE IS BLUEBOX</h2>
    
    <div class="box2">
    </div>
   </div>
    
   <div>
    <div class="box"></div>
    <p class="long-text">
    Responsive design ensures that websites work well on mobile phones, tablets,
    and desktop screens. CSS positioning plays a major role in modern layouts.
    (Copy this paragraph multiple times to create scroll.)
    </p>
  </div>
  <!-- Fixed footer -->
  <div class="footer">
    This is fixed footer
  </div>

  <!-- Fixed button -->
  <button class="contact-btn">Contact Me</button>

</body>
</html>